{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_chapter4", "label": "Chapter 4 \u2014 The periodic table is not a closed index", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_e_periodic_table_36", "label": "E(periodic table) = 36 \u2014 the gaps in the short periods", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not a defect in the periodic table but a fact about what its coordinates can carry: period and group locate an element and do not encode why period 1 has room for two."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_reconstruction_operator", "label": "\u211b \u2014 value sets and monotone envelopes, and E(X) = |\u211b(X)| \u2212 |X|", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No outside knowledge enters: \u211b(X) is what a reader could reconstruct from the cells alone."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_helium_placement", "label": "E is a property of where helium is drawn \u2014 36 at group 18, 20 at group 2", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The mechanism is the envelope \u03c6\u0302(group | period \u2264 1); E measures what the placement choice costs to specify, and the difference is sixteen cells."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_janet_left_step", "label": "The Janet left-step table is closed \u2014 E = 0 over 120 cells", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_e36_undefended", "label": "E(periodic table) = 36 carries no independent defence", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The order and geometry routes are one computation written twice, because the table has no separately stated constraints to check the recovered ones against."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_nuclide_chart_defect", "label": "The measured nuclide chart's E = 9 \u2014 pairing and clustering, counted", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The drawn band's E = 0 is a theorem from idempotence, not a finding about nuclei; the measurement is the other object. The nine cells are the pairing and clustering terms of the mass formula, and they persist unchanged at four cutoffs."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_ionization_refusals", "label": "First-ionization monotonicity refusals \u2014 s\u00b2\u2192p\u00b9 and p\u00b3\u2192p\u2074", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A retrodiction, not a discovery; what earns it a place is that it is mechanical \u2014 where an index refuses, a mechanism is entering that the coordinates do not carry."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_calendar_seven", "label": "The calendar's seven \u2014 E(X) = 7 is the price of keeping January first", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Non-closure is not always a fault; it is sometimes a purchase. The repaired calendar is self-defining and unusable, and the book supplies the price tag rather than the verdict."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_composition_as_time", "label": "Composition as time \u2014 a coordinate the book already carried, read as an order", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_observation_frame_arrow", "label": "The arrow is a property of what the observer takes as the starting state", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Occupancy never rises in the empty-destination frame; represent occupied destinations and 31.6% of steps run the other way. Neither reading is wrong, and observation selects between the two."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter4_periodic_table_figure_4_1", "label": "Figure 4.1 \u2014 external definition cost of seven indices", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter4-periodic-table.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author"